        "howNativesThink": "Native speakers associate 'caramelize' with patient culinary craftsmanship that cannot be rushed. Describing an ingredient as 'caramelized' on a restaurant menu (such as caramelized onions or caramelized pear tart) conveys artisan care, rich umami-sweet flavor, and premium quality. People instinctively know that high heat burns, whereas slow heat caramelizes.",
