        "whenNotToUse": "Do not use 'caramelize' to mean simply scorching, charring, or burning food. In rigorous food chemistry, do not confuse caramelization (pure sugar pyrolysis) with the Maillard reaction (reaction between amino acids and reducing sugars in meats/breads), although everyday culinary speech sometimes blurs them.",
