        "howNativesThink": "Native speakers treat \"cream\" both as a basic beverage condiment (\"How do you take your coffee? Cream and sugar?\") and as a sensory hallmark of culinary richness and luxury. In professional catering and dining, offering fresh dairy cream rather than powdered or non-dairy substitutes is an immediate indicator of food quality.",
        "mentalImage": "A miniature silver pitcher pouring a thick, velvety stream of heavy dairy cream into a dark, freshly brewed cup of roast coffee, creating swirling marble patterns across the dark surface.",
        "whenNotToUse": "Do not confuse cream with regular milk (which has significantly lower fat content and a lighter body) or processed plant-based creamers unless explicitly designated (e.g., oat creamer).",
