        "howNativesThink": "Native speakers consider \"crispy\" one of the most effective sensory descriptors on a restaurant menu. It instantly evokes the satisfying sound and texture of golden fried chicken, thin-crust pizza, or freshly cooked bacon. In dining contexts, \"crispy\" is synonymous with culinary freshness, while its opposite, \"soggy\", signifies poor preparation or excessive holding time.",
