        "howNativesThink": "Native speakers associate croissant with European caf\u00e9 charm, butter-laden indulgence, and upscale morning hospitality. Rather than seeing it as plain bread, natives view it as a treat or an elevated breakfast standard. In corporate catering, providing croissants signals that the host went beyond basic bagels or grocery donuts. When biting in, there is an expectation of a shatteringly crisp exterior yielding to light, steamy, honeycomb butter layers.",
        "mentalImage": "A wicker basket lined with a crisp white linen cloth on a polished granite conference sideboard, overflowing with golden-brown, curved croissants whose delicate flaky layers crackle as a meeting attendee picks one up with silver serving tongs beside bowls of artisanal berry preserves.",
