        "howNativesThink": "To a native speaker, 'cup' is both a universal household object and a social catalyst. Asking a colleague 'Want to grab a cup of coffee?' is the universal corporate code for an informal 15-minute one-on-one catch-up, brainstorming session, or decompression chat. In dining, 'a cup' denotes an explicit portion size for soups or chowders, distinct from a larger 'bowl'. Natives distinguish between a 'cup' (usually smaller, often with a saucer or disposable paper) and a 'mug' (heavy, straight-sided, handle-held, used informally at one's desk).",
        "mentalImage": "A gleaming commercial espresso station on an office breakroom counter, where an employee places an ivory ceramic cup beneath dual brass spouts, watching rich dark espresso drip smoothly into the cup as steam rises against the stainless steel backsplash.",
