        "howNativesThink": "To native speakers, glassware is an uncountable collective noun covering all beverage containers (wine stems, champagne flutes, water goblets, tumblers, and highballs). In restaurant and banquet operations, polishing glassware under steam with lint-free towels is a hallmark of proper hospitality staging. Native speakers instinctively distinguish glassware from flatware (cutlery) and chinaware (plates and bowls).",
        "mentalImage": "A banquet server holding a stemmed crystal wine glass by the foot over warm steam, buffing it to a streak-free shine with a white lint-free microfiber cloth beneath warm dining room chandeliers, flanked by stacked wash racks of sparkling water goblets.",
