        "commonMistakes": "Learners frequently mispronounce the word by articulating the silent terminal letter 'b', producing /l\u00e6mb/ instead of /l\u00e6m/. In standard English, the final 'b' following 'm' has been completely silent since late Middle English; the vocal tract stops at the bilabial nasal /m/.",
