        "howNativesThink": "To native speakers, 'lettuce' is the quintessential fresh green vegetable\u2014synonymous with crispness, hydration, and clean eating. It is the architectural foundation of salads and an indispensable sandwich layer that provides textural crunch while acting as a physical moisture barrier keeping bread from absorbing wet condiments. In workplace dining, the freshness of lettuce serves as an instant quality litmus test: crisp, vibrant green leaves signal diligent kitchen hygiene and fresh inventory, whereas limp, pinkish-brown edges ('rust') immediately repel diners. Culturally, 'head of lettuce' is the default shopping unit, and 'lettuce wraps' represent modern health-conscious or low-carbohydrate dining.",
