        "howNativesThink": "To native speakers, 'mocktail' represents social inclusivity and mindful hospitality. In past eras, non-drinkers at professional events were relegated to club soda with a lime or tap water, which felt exclusionary. A mocktail allows attendees to hold a beautifully garnished, complex drink and participate fully in toasts and networking without consuming alcohol, experiencing hangovers, or violating company conduct rules or personal beliefs (sobriety, religion, designated driving, wellness). In modern HR and corporate event planning, providing signature mocktails is standard best practice.",
