        "evolution": "Originating as an ancient weaving term for threading a loom and a military term for ranks of soldiers, '\u014drd\u014d' passed into Old French as 'ordre' to signify orderly arrangement and religious brotherhoods. In Middle English, it signified regular arrangement and authoritative instructions. By the 18th and 19th centuries, with the rise of commercial inns, taverns, and early restaurants, 'order' evolved to designate a customer's specific itemized request for food or drink to be prepared and served by the establishment.",
