        "commonMistakes": "Learners often mispronounce the short open vowel /\u0251\u02d0/ (in General American) or /\u0252/ (in Received Pronunciation) as /\u0254\u02d0/ (sounding like 'port' or 'pawn') or /o\u028a/ (sounding like 'boat'). Additionally, learners frequently confuse 'pot' with 'pan'. A 'pot' has high, deep vertical sides and two loop handles (designed for liquids, soups, boiling, and simmering), whereas a 'pan' is shallow with a single long handle (designed for frying, searing, and saut\u00e9ing). In beverage contexts, learners sometimes mistakenly say 'a cup of coffee' when referring to the brewing vessel rather than the individual serving ('a pot of coffee').",
        "ipa": "/p\u0251\u02d0t/",
        "stressPattern": "\u25cf",
        "syllableBreakdown": "pot"
