        "howNativesThink": "To a native speaker, a 'saucer' instantly evokes traditional, civilized tea or coffee service as opposed to casual drinking from a heavy ceramic mug. The pairing 'cup and saucer' is an inseparable linguistic doublet. Culturally, eyes 'as big as saucers' is a classic idiom indicating astonishment or shock, while 'flying saucer' refers to science-fiction UFOs due to their disk-like silhouette. In hospitality, serving a hot beverage without a saucer is seen as informal or incomplete in upscale dining.",
