        "howNativesThink": "Native speakers regard 'seafood' as a healthy, light, and upscale dining choice, strongly associated with coastal dining, fine wine pairings, and luxury dining experiences (such as oyster bars or lobster dinners). However, in professional hospitality and corporate event management, 'seafood' immediately prompts high operational alertness around two critical issues: absolute freshness (due to the rapid risk of histamine toxicity and bacterial spoilage) and severe food allergies (shellfish is one of the top food allergens worldwide). Consequently, native event hosts always require attendees to specify whether they have shellfish or finfish allergies.",
