        "commonMistakes": "Learners often shorten the tense long vowel /i\u02d0/ to a lax /\u026a/ (pronouncing it like 'sitting' /\u02c8s\u026at\u026a\u014b/ instead of 'seating' /\u02c8si\u02d0t\u026a\u014b/), which causes confusion between the physical act of resting on a chair ('sitting') and the designated arrangement, capacity, or dining shift ('seating'). Another frequent error is treating 'seating' in its furniture or capacity sense as a plural count noun (saying 'we need more seatings' instead of 'we need more seating' or 'more seats'). Note that 'seating' takes a plural form only when denoting multiple scheduled banquet shifts (e.g., 'the 6:00 PM and 8:30 PM seatings').",
        "ipa": "/\u02c8si\u02d0.t\u026a\u014b/",
